{#
    `.. [NAME] …` — a work being cited, at the foot of the page.

    Its own name rather than the footnote's: a footnote is an aside the author
    wrote and this is somebody else's work, the source tells them apart, and
    two names is what lets either be set differently later.

    Renamed off the core's `.citation` for the reason `footnote.html.twig`
    gives — a class on a page this system draws is a name this system defines.
#}
<div class="sds-citation{% if node.classes %} {{ node.classesString }}{% endif %}" id="{{ node.anchor }}">
    <div class="sds-citation__label">[{{ node.name }}]</div>
    <div class="sds-citation__content">
        {%- for child in node.children -%}
            {{ renderNode(child) }}
        {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
</div>
